  },
  {
    "text": "USB OUTPUT ON/OFF ",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "Once the product is turned on, the USB ports are automatically enabled for power output, allowing you to charge your devices.",
    "source_page": 9,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "CAUTION",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "USB-C1 and USB-C2 are USB-PD Power Source 3 (PS3) high-power output ports. If the connected user device or accessory does not meet safety requirements, there may be a fire risk. Before using these ports, ensure that the connected device or accessory has fire safety protection. Only connect the Jackery Explorer 300D to devices or accessories that comply with clauses 6.3, 6.4, and 6.5 of IEC/EN/UL 62368-1 (or other equivalent standards). To obtain maximum output power, use the official Jackery USB-C to USB-C 5A cable (20V DC/5A, 100W; 28V DC/5A, 140W).",
    "source_page": 9,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 0.9885,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "DC 12V OUTPUT ON/OFF ",
    "source_page": 9,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "Prerequisite: The product is turned on.",
    "source_page": 9,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "* The product can charge your car battery using the Jackery 12V automobile battery charging cable, which is sold separately and available on our website.",
    "source_page": 9,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "CAUTION",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "The DC 12V outlet (cigarette lighter port) is only compatible with 12V car batteries and not suitable for 24V systems. Do not start the car while the product is charging the car battery through the 12V DC output port (cigarette lighter port), as this may damage the product. This feature is intended for emergency use only and cannot charge a dead or damaged car battery.",
    "source_page": 9,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "ENERGY SAVING MODE ",
    "source_page": 10,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "To prevent unnecessary battery consumption from forgetting to turn off the output, the product enables Energy Saving Mode by default. If no device is connected or the connected device's power consumption is below 2W for 6 hours, the product will automatically turn off all outputs and then power off. To disable the energy saving mode, press the main power button three times. The product will not automatically turn off the output.",
    "source_page": 10,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "NOTE",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Energy Saving Mode resumes previous state after power-on. Manual switching is required for mode changes.",
    "source_page": 10,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "LED LIGHT ON/OFF ",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "The LED light has two modes: Light mode and SOS mode. The default setting is Light mode. In any mode, press and hold the LED light button to turn off the light.",
