  },
  {
    "text": "Green energy first: We advocate to use the green energy first. This product supports two modes of charging at the same time: solar charging and USB-C charging. When USB-C charging and solar charging are turned on at the same time, the product will give priority to solar charging and both methods will be used to charge the battery at the maximum permissible power.",
    "source_page": 11,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "Fully charge the product before its first use.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "NOTE",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "The recommended charging temperature for the product ranges from 32°F to 113°F (0°C to 45°C), and the discharging temperature ranges from 5°F to 113°F (-15°C to 45°C). Operating the product beyond this temperature range may restrict its charging and discharging capabilities, or even prevent it from charging or discharging. The charging power and battery capacity of the product may vary due to temperature fluctuations.",
    "source_page": 11,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "USB-C CHARGING (140W MAX) ",
    "source_page": 12,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "Prepare a wall charger. Remove the two-in-one carry handle, which is also a USB-C cable. Connect it to the product’s USB-C1 port and a power outlet.",
    "source_page": 12,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "CAUTION",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "When charging through the USB-C port, this product supports up to 140W, which requires a PD charger and cable that both support 140W.",
    "source_page": 12,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "SOLAR CHARGING (100W MAX) ",
    "source_page": 12,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Jackery Explorer 300D has one DC8020 input port, which supports direct connection of a solar panel.",
    "source_page": 12,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "It is recommended to use a Jackery solar panel to charge the product. Ensure that the open-circuit voltage (V oc ) of the solar panel falls within the Jackery Explorer 300D's DC input voltage range (16V–28V). Jackery is not responsible for any damage or loss resulting from the use of third-party solar panels.",
    "source_page": 12,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "CAR CHARGING (96W MAX) ",
    "source_page": 13,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "text": "This product can be charged using a 12V car charger. Ensure that the car charger and the car cigarette lighter provide a good connection.",
    "source_page": 13,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "* The car charging cable is sold separately.",
    "source_page": 13,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "CAUTION",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Please start the vehicle before charging your power station. If the vehicle is running on bumpy roads, it is forbidden to use the car charger in case it causes non-standard operation. The Company will not be responsible for any loss caused by non-standard operation. Vehicle charging is only applicable to vehicles with 12V DC, not 24V DC. Please do not charge this product in 24V vehicle to avoid personal injury and property loss.",
    "source_page": 13,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Store the product in a dry clean place with proper ventilation. Storage temperature and humidity:",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "If this product is stored for a long period of time (3 months - 6 months) with the power depleted, it may become unchargeable. To prevent this and maintain battery health, it is recommended to check and recharge the product every three months and perform a full charge and discharge cycle at least once every 6 to 12 months.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "If any of the following fault codes appear, follow the listed corrective actions to resolve the issue. If fault persists, please contact Jackery Customer Support.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "p"
  },
  {
    "text": "Error Code",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "th"
  },
  {
    "text": "Corrective Measures",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "th"
  },
  {
    "text": "F0",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Restart the product.",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F1",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Contact Jackery Customer Support.",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F2",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Contact Jackery Customer Support.",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F3",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Restart the product.",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F4",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Connect the product to loads to discharge its battery until the fault disappears.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F5",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Charge the product via USB-C or solar panel until the fault disappears.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F6",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Contact Jackery Customer Support.",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F7",
    "source_page": 15,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "1. Remove all DC inputs from the product. 2. If you charge the product via a solar panel, check the open-circuited voltage (V oc ) of the connected solar panel.The product allows a maximum DC input voltage of 28V. 3. Restart the product and keep it idle. Wait until the fault disappears.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F8",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Contact Jackery Customer Support.",
    "source_page": 17,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "F9",
    "source_page": 18,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
  },
  {
    "text": "Remove the load connected to the DC 12V/USB ports of the product. Wait until the fault disappears.",
    "source_page": 14,
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0,
    "dom_tag": "td"
